'' T59, RUN: '#pragma private' makes a procedure written under it private, as fbc's
'' FBOPTION_PROCPUBLIC does -- Helper in a.bas is a.bas's own, and b.bas's Helper links
'' beside it. tiko kept the pragma's macro and ignored its meaning, so the two collided.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/pragma-private/a.bas tests/codegen/src/pragma-private/b.bas -o tests/codegen/pragmapriv.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/pragmapriv.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  2 7
